=== NOTES ===
1. `bracketFloors(['$12,400 or less', '$12,400'])` is valid `[0, 12400]`: bottom bracket up to $12,400, next bracket over $12,400. Updated the existing `table.test.ts` rejection expectation to `deepEqual(..., [0, 12400])`; implementation unchanged. The remaining cases still cover empty input, non-first ceilings, non-ascending floors, and unparsable input.
2. Fixed the IRS row-0 quote to the page-verbatim span `The lowest rate is 10% for incomes of single individuals with incomes of $12,400 or less ($24,800 for married couples filing jointly)` (about 133 chars, under the 150 limit). It contains the row-0 printed values `10%`, `$12,400 or less`, and `$24,800` exactly.
3. `answerQuestion` largest/smallest now uses `bracketFloors` over the column values when `gen.brackets.enabled` is true and `q.columnIndex === gen.brackets.overColumnIndex`. Lookup still returns the printed cell string; largest/smallest compare floors and return the printed winner string, or null when floors are null. Added a `table.test.ts` bracket-column case covering largest, smallest, lookup passthrough, and a descending null.
4. Isolated the DT-07 descending-thresholds negative: it now drops the ceiling row and reverses the remaining pure-number rows, and probes lookup plus largest-on-rate-column so DT-04 and DT-05 stay green. It asserts exactly `['DT-07']` with affected `/rows/0/values/1/value`. No validator file changes were needed.
